<http://data.silknow.org/object/a502f84c-fdef-325c-90cb-25d8cb031c0d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "White silk satin wedding dress with overdress of embroidered flounced net lace, white satin bonnet, a bonnet-veil of applied bobbin lace motifs on net, a handkerchief of white embroidered cambric, a pair of garters of fine canvas embroidered with rosebuds, and a fan  with a leaf of Brussels lace initialled H.B. (for Henrietta Bell) on mother of pearl sticks"@en , "White satin with overdress of embroidered net lace and accessories; England; worn in 1848"@en ;
